Lane's Lexicon  (lane-xml/)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Edward William Lane, "An Arabic-English Lexicon" (London, 1863–1893).
The underlying work is in the public domain.

Digital TEI XML text via the Perseus Digital Library and the corrected
"Lane's Lexicon" project (https://laneslexicon.github.io/), whose XML is
distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike license
(CC BY-SA). Because this data is ShareAlike, any redistribution of the
Lane portion (including derivatives) must remain under CC BY-SA and credit
Perseus / the Lane's Lexicon project.

